<title>FRANCE: Total Chemicals sees currencies boosting sales.</title>
<headline>Total Chemicals sees currencies boosting sales.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jean-Pierre Seeuws, managing director of Total's chemical division, said on Monday that the present currency situation would boost 1997 sales by between three and four percent.</p>
<p>&quot;In the first few months of 1997, the currency situation, with especially the pound sterling and the dollar, is favourable to us,&quot; he told a news conference.</p>
<p>He maintained that the division would reach total sales of 30 billion francs in the year 2000 against 24.6 billion in 1996. He said this would come from internal and external growth.</p>
</text>
